      whether for free, for a fee, or for any other consideration;
  (e) Use the Software, in whole or in part, to develop, train, fine-tune,
      benchmark, evaluate, or operate any competing product, dataset, large
      language model, embedding model, or other machine-learning system;
  (f) Use the Software to produce content, prompts, or weights that are
      then redistributed in a manner that would have been a Restriction had
      they been part of the Software directly;
  (g) Use the Software in any manner that violates the OpenHours Terms of
      Service or Privacy Policy;
  (h) Remove, alter, obscure, or fail to preserve copyright, license,
      attribution, or proprietary notices, including the names of the
      Maintainers;
  (i) Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise attempt to
      derive the source code of any compiled portion of the Software,
      except to the extent applicable law expressly prohibits this
      restriction and only to the minimum extent so required;
  (j) Use any OpenHours trademark, service mark, logo, trade dress, or
      domain name except with the prior written consent of OpenHours, or
      as permitted by Section 8;
  (k) Misrepresent that You, or any product or service offered by You, are
      affiliated with, sponsored by, endorsed by, or authorized by
      OpenHours or any Maintainer;
  (l) Circumvent or attempt to circumvent any technical, contractual, or
      access control imposed on the Software or the Service.

