11. Security Disclosure
================================================================================

If You discover a security vulnerability in the Software or the Service,
please report it privately to security@openhours.me before any public
disclosure. The Maintainers will acknowledge a good-faith report within a
reasonable time and will not pursue legal action under this license against
a researcher who:

  (a) reports a vulnerability privately and in good faith;
  (b) does not access user data beyond what is strictly necessary to
      demonstrate the vulnerability;
  (c) does not modify, destroy, exfiltrate, or retain user data;
  (d) does not degrade or disrupt the Service; and
  (e) gives the Maintainers a reasonable opportunity to remediate before
      any public disclosure.

This Section 11 is not a bug-bounty program and does not commit the
Maintainers to compensate any researcher.

